From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:40:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,tristar-charger: Take PMU
 events as interrupts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The charger used to own the D2365 PMU event block and the PMU line itself.
The PMIC GPIO node is now the interrupt controller for that block, so the
charger no longer describes the block and instead consumes the events it
needs: the PMU line itself first (the controller's interrupt 240, run
before the block is read, where the charger withdraws a grant), then ADC
conversion complete, then every event that can signal a change of the
attached source.

J71t ledger 5.1 (one shared D2365 event interrupt controller).

Reported-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml   | 40 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
index 629dbaf92..521554c70 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ description: |
   Charging on Apple devices whose Lightning port uses a Tristar (NXP CBTL1610)
   port controller and a D2365-family PMIC. The node is a child of the PMIC.
   It identifies the attached source through the Tristar and the PMIC ADC and
-  sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot leaves at 100 mA.
+  sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot leaves at 100 mA. PMU events
+  come from the PMIC's event interrupt controller (the PMIC GPIO node).
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: power-supply.yaml#
@@ -29,19 +30,24 @@ properties:
     items:
       - description: Charger status register bank.
       - description: Charger control register bank.
-      - description: PMU event register block, read to acknowledge.
       - description: ADC register bank.
 
   reg-names:
     items:
       - const: status
       - const: control
-      - const: event
       - const: adc
 
   interrupts:
-    maxItems: 1
-    description: PMU event interrupt, active low.
+    minItems: 3
+    maxItems: 16
+    description: |
+      From the PMIC's event interrupt controller. The first is the PMU event
+      line itself, which runs before the events are read: the charger
+      withdraws a grant there, before it knows which event it was. The
+      second is ADC conversion complete. Every further entry is an event
+      that can signal a change of the attached source (attach, detach,
+      charger state); any of them starts a new identification.
 
   apple,tristar:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
@@ -78,11 +84,29 @@ examples:
         #address-cells = <1>;
         #size-cells = <1>;
 
+        pmu_gpio: gpio {
+            compatible = "apple,d2365-pmic-gpio";
+            gpio-controller;
+            #gpio-cells = <2>;
+            interrupt-controller;
+            #interrupt-cells = <2>;
+            interrupts = <38 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+        };
+
         charger@180 {
             compatible = "apple,j71b-tristar-charger", "apple,tristar-charger";
-            reg = <0x180 0x10>, <0xa00 0x04>, <0x140 0x1e>, <0x4000 0x03>;
-            reg-names = "status", "control", "event", "adc";
-            interrupts = <38 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+            reg = <0x180 0x10>, <0xa00 0x04>, <0x4000 0x03>;
+            reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+            interrupt-parent = <&pmu_gpio>;
+            interrupts = <240 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <176 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <16 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <40 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <41 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <42 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <43 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <72 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+                         <77 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
             apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
             input-current-limit-microamp = <2400000>;
         };
